.Dd June 18, 2026
.Dt PDSELF 2
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm pdself
.Nd create a process descriptor for the calling process
.Sh LIBRARY
.Lb libc
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In sys/procdesc.h
.Ft int
.Fn pdself "int *fdp" "int flags"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Fn pdself
system call creates a process descriptor for the calling process and
stores the resulting file descriptor in the integer pointed to by
.Fa fdp .
This is a capability-mode-only system call
.Pq Dv SYF_CAPREQUIRED ;
it returns
.Er ENOTCAPABLE
when called outside
.Xr capsicum 4
capability mode.
.Pp
The resulting process descriptor can be passed over a
.Xr unix 4
domain socket to a supervisor process, which can then use
.Xr pdkill 2 ,
.Xr pdwait 2 ,
and
.Xr pdgetpid 2
to manage the caller without requiring PIDs or traditional UNIX
permission checks.
.Pp
The
.Fa flags
argument may contain the following values:
.Bl -tag -width PD_CLOEXEC
.It Dv PD_CLOEXEC
Set close-on-exec on the process descriptor.
.It Dv PD_DAEMON
Do not terminate the process when an external holder closes the last
reference to the descriptor.
.El
.Pp
At most one process descriptor may exist per process.
If the calling process already has a process descriptor
(either from
.Fn pdself
or from being created via
.Xr pdfork 2 ) ,
.Fn pdself
fails with
.Er EBUSY .
.Ss Close semantics
Process descriptors created by
.Fn pdself
have the
.Dv PDF_SELF
flag set, which modifies the behavior of
.Xr close 2
on the last reference:
.Bl -bullet
.It
If the described process itself closes the last reference, the
descriptor is silently detached.
The process is not killed and not reparented.
.It
If any other process closes the last reference, normal process
descriptor semantics apply: the described process receives
.Dv SIGKILL
and is reparented to its reaper (unless
.Dv PD_DAEMON
was also set).
.It
If the close is not the last reference (other file descriptors or
in-flight SCM_RIGHTS copies exist), nothing happens regardless of
who closes it.
.El
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Rv -std
.Sh ERRORS
The
.Fn pdself
system call fails if:
.Bl -tag -width Er
.It Bq Er EBUSY
The calling process already has a process descriptor.
.It Bq Er EINVAL
The
.Fa flags
argument contains invalid flags.
.It Bq Er ENOTCAPABLE
The caller is not in capability mode.
.It Bq Er EMFILE
The per-process file descriptor limit has been reached.
.It Bq Er ENFILE
The system file descriptor limit has been reached.
.It Bq Er ENOMEM
Insufficient memory to allocate the process descriptor.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr cap_enter 2 ,
.Xr close 2 ,
.Xr pdcmp 2 ,
.Xr pdfork 2 ,
.Xr pdgetpid 2 ,
.Xr pdkill 2 ,
.Xr pdwait 2 ,
.Xr capsicum 4 ,
.Xr procdesc 4
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Fn pdself
system call first appeared in
.Fx 16.0 .
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Kory Heard
